{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HjRnnavVMFAjzU8MdzWVdB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tslug: pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\n3\tstatus: draft\n4\tcreated_at: 2026-11-23\n5\tcompleted_at:\n6\tsupersedes:\n7\tdepends_on: \n8\tremediates:\n9\tpriority: 2\n10\tcomponents: pose-mcp\n11\ttask_type: bugfix\n12\tsurface: standard\n13\tdelivers: capability:validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t# Spec: pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\n17\t\n18\t## 1. Intent\n19\t\n20\t### Goal\n21\tMake the engine's own Git reads during `pose validate` and `pose check`, such as the provenance status of `validate`, never rewrite `.git/index` or take index locks in the validated checkout.\n22\t\n23\t### Business value\n24\tIn Harne8 the governance read view of `instance-health-composite` failed intermittently with `review inputs changed during operation: .git` because concurrent reads refreshed the index stat cache. The Harne8 bugfix `harne8-validation-reads-leave-root-index-alone` fixed the instance's own scripts and left this engine part as its follow-up F1.\n25\t\n26\t### Constraints\n27\tReads keep their results. Stale stat caches may cost time, never correctness.\n28\t\n29\t### Non-goals\n30\tChanging which files are compared.\n31\t\n32\t## 2. Requirements\n33\t\n34\t### Functional\n35\t- R1: Every status, diff and ls-files read the engine makes for validation provenance, material cleanliness and readiness checks shall run with optional locks disabled, and a comparison with the work tree shall be read from `git status` instead of `git diff`, so none rewrites `.git/index` or takes its lock (D1).\n36\t- R2: A regression test shall run those reads over a checkout with a stale stat cache and prove `.git/index` byte-identical afterwards.\n37\t- R3: A concurrency test shall run those reads together on one checkout while a reader watches `.git/index` and its lock, and see neither change (D2).\n38\t\n39\t### Non-functional\n40\tExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n41\t\n42\t### Security\n43\tNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n44\t\n45\t### Compatibility\n46\tRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n47\t\n48\t## 3. Technical Plan\n49\t\n50\t### Affected areas\n51\t`pose-mcp`: the engine's Git command constructor (`gitCommandContext`), work-tree read helpers (`git_worktree_reads.go`), and the work-tree diffs of `check` (ready transitions), `validate` scope selection, `report` and the review history ledger.\n52\t\n53\t### Artifacts\n54\t- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\n55\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\n56\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n57\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n58\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n59\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n60\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n61\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n62\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n63\t\n64\t### Delivery targets\n65\t- capability:validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\n66\t\n67\t### Accepted limits\n68\t- L1: A Git command the engine runs through another constructor, or a tool a validation step runs, can still refresh the index. Accepted because every engine read goes through `gitCommandContext`, and what a step runs is the project's command, which the Harne8 bugfix of its own scripts already covers.\n69\t- L2: A path changed both in the commits since a base and in the work tree is compared with the base by content only, so a change of its mode alone back to the base's is not seen. Accepted because only scope selection and `report --since` read it, and listing such a path runs or reports more, never less.\n70\t\n71\t### API/contract changes\n72\tNone: the reads answer as before; only where their stat refresh is written changes.\n73\t\n74\t### Data/storage changes\n75\tNone.\n76\t\n77\t### Technical risks\n78\t`git status` must not take the index lock: every engine command carries `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, which the tests prove by mutation.\n79\t\n80\t## 4. Tasks\n81\t\n82\t### Planning\n83\t- [x] Confirm the requirements against the current engine before starting.\n84\t\n85\t### Implementation\n86\t- [x] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n87\t\n88\t### Validation\n89\t- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n90\t\n91\t## 5. Decisions\n92\t\n93\t### Decision D1\n94\t- Basis: R1\n95\tR1 as drafted asked for `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false`. Measured on a stale stat cache, `git diff --name-only HEAD` rewrites the index even with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, and with `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false` it lists a file whose stat alone changed, which breaks the constraint that reads keep their results. `git status` with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` refreshes in memory and writes nothing. So every engine Git command carries `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, and a comparison with the work tree is read from `git status --no-renames --untracked-files=no` (`WorktreeChanges`), mapped to the change `git diff HEAD --name-status` names. A comparison with an older base adds the commits' own diff, which touches no index, and a path in both is kept only when the work tree still differs from the base by content (`git hash-object`, which writes nothing without `-w`; a submodule by its checked-out commit), so the names equal `git diff --name-only <base>`. A first version ran the diff over a private copy of the index (`GIT_INDEX_FILE`); the full suite refused it, since a dry run must create no file at all, temporary ones included (`TestUpdatePreviewHasNoPhysicalMutationEvents`).\n96\t\n97\t### Decision D2\n98\t- Basis: R3\n99\tR3 as drafted ran `validate` and `check --strict` together. The property they broke is that a reader saw `.git` change under it; the test runs the reads those commands make, concurrently, while a reader watches `.git/index` and `index.lock`, which shows the property directly and runs in under a second instead of a full validation.\n100\t\n101\t## 6. Validation\n102\t\n103\t### Strategy\n104\tEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n105\t\n106\t### Deterministic checks\n107\t\n108\t#### Test\n109\t- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n110\t\n111\t### Execution log\n112\t- 2026-11-26: `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` in `gitCommandContext`; the work-tree diffs of the ready-transition read, scope selection, `report --since` and the review history ledger read `git status` (`WorktreeChanges`, `WorktreeChangedNames`). `TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone`, `TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex` and `TestWorktreeReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone` fail with each guard mutated out (the optional-locks setting, each caller's `git diff` restored, the content comparison); the last also checks the answers equal `git diff` for a commit since the base, a modified, a deleted and a staged-new file. A first private-index version was refused by the full suite (D1).\n113\t\n114\t### Results summary\n115\tThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n116\t\n117\t### Requirement trace\n118\t- R1 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone, test:TestWorktreeReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone\n119\t- R2 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone\n120\t- R3 [satisfied] test:TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex\n121\t\n122\t### Known gaps\n123\tNone.\n124\t\n125\t## 7. Final Report\n126\t\n127\t### Delivered scope\n128\tThe engine's Git reads during `validate`, `check` and `report` no longer rewrite `.git/index` or take its lock, and keep their answers.\n129\t\n130\t### Files and modules changed\n131\t`pose-mcp` Git command construction and the work-tree diffs of check, validate scope, report and the review history ledger.\n132\t\n133\t### Validation executed\n134\t`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n135\t\n136\t### Residual risks\n137\tL1 and L2 above.\n138\t\n139\t### Follow-ups\n140\tNone.\n141\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"2e117afd-c0c8-4644-9b47-9966b2cfa282","timestamp":"2026-11-26T13:38:48.033Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-11b0b7dffb/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md","content":"---\nslug: pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\nstatus: draft\ncreated_at: 2026-11-23\ncompleted_at:\nsupersedes:\ndepends_on: \nremediates:\npriority: 2\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: bugfix\nsurface: standard\ndelivers: capability:validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nMake the engine's own Git reads during `pose validate` and `pose check`, such as the provenance status of `validate`, never rewrite `.git/index` or take index locks in the validated checkout.\n\n### Business value\nIn Harne8 the governance read view of `instance-health-composite` failed intermittently with `review inputs changed during operation: .git` because concurrent reads refreshed the index stat cache. The Harne8 bugfix `harne8-validation-reads-leave-root-index-alone` fixed the instance's own scripts and left this engine part as its follow-up F1.\n\n### Constraints\nReads keep their results. Stale stat caches may cost time, never correctness.\n\n### Non-goals\nChanging which files are compared.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: Every status, diff and ls-files read the engine makes for validation provenance, material cleanliness and readiness checks shall run with optional locks disabled, and a comparison with the work tree shall be read from `git status` instead of `git diff`, so none rewrites `.git/index` or takes its lock (D1).\n- R2: A regression test shall run those reads over a checkout with a stale stat cache and prove `.git/index` byte-identical afterwards.\n- R3: A concurrency test shall run those reads together on one checkout while a reader watches `.git/index` and its lock, and see neither change (D2).\n\n### Non-functional\nExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n\n### Security\nNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n\n### Compatibility\nRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n`pose-mcp`: the engine's Git command constructor (`gitCommandContext`), work-tree read helpers (`git_worktree_reads.go`), and the work-tree diffs of `check` (ready transitions), `validate` scope selection, `report` and the review history ledger.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n\n### Delivery targets\n- capability:validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\n\n### Accepted limits\n- L1: A Git command the engine runs through another constructor, or a tool a validation step runs, can still refresh the index. Accepted because every engine read goes through `gitCommandContext`, and what a step runs is the project's command, which the Harne8 bugfix of its own scripts already covers.\n- L2: A path changed both in the commits since a base and in the work tree is compared with the base by content only, so a change of its mode alone back to the base's is not seen. Accepted because only scope selection and `report --since` read it, and listing such a path runs or reports more, never less.\n\n### API/contract changes\nNone: the reads answer as before; only where their stat refresh is written changes.\n\n### Data/storage changes\nNone.\n\n### Technical risks\n`git status` must not take the index lock: every engine command carries `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, which the tests prove by mutation.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Planning\n- [x] Confirm the requirements against the current engine before starting.\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n\n### Validation\n- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Basis: R1\nR1 as drafted asked for `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false`. Measured on a stale stat cache, `git diff --name-only HEAD` rewrites the index even with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, and with `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false` it lists a file whose stat alone changed, which breaks the constraint that reads keep their results. `git status` with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` refreshes in memory and writes nothing. So every engine Git command carries `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, and a comparison with the work tree is read from `git status --no-renames --untracked-files=no` (`WorktreeChanges`), mapped to the change `git diff HEAD --name-status` names. A comparison with an older base adds the commits' own diff, which touches no index, and a path in both is kept only when the work tree still differs from the base by content (`git hash-object`, which writes nothing without `-w`; a submodule by its checked-out commit), so the names equal `git diff --name-only <base>`. A first version ran the diff over a private copy of the index (`GIT_INDEX_FILE`); the full suite refused it, since a dry run must create no file at all, temporary ones included (`TestUpdatePreviewHasNoPhysicalMutationEvents`).\n\n### Decision D2\n- Basis: R3\nR3 as drafted ran `validate` and `check --strict` together. The property they broke is that a reader saw `.git` change under it; the test runs the reads those commands make, concurrently, while a reader watches `.git/index` and `index.lock`, which shows the property directly and runs in under a second instead of a full validation.\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Execution log\n- 2026-11-26: `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` in `gitCommandContext`; the work-tree diffs of the ready-transition read, scope selection, `report --since` and the review history ledger read `git status` (`WorktreeChanges`, `WorktreeChangedNames`). `TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone`, `TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex` and `TestWorktreeReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone` fail with each guard mutated out (the optional-locks setting, each caller's `git diff` restored, the content comparison); the last also checks the answers equal `git diff` for a commit since the base, a modified, a deleted and a staged-new file. A first private-index version was refused by the full suite (D1).\n\n### Results summary\nThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone, test:TestWorktreeReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex\n\n### Known gaps\nNone.\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nThe engine's Git reads during `validate`, `check` and `report` no longer rewrite `.git/index` or take its lock, and keep their answers.\n\n### Files and modules changed\n`pose-mcp` Git command construction and the work-tree diffs of check, validate scope, report and the review history ledger.\n\n### Validation executed\n`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n\n### Residual risks\nL1 and L2 above.\n\n### Follow-ups\nNone.\n","numLines":141,"startLine":1,"totalLines":141}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HjRnnavVMFAjzU8MdzWVdB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
